  "src.muslim-1218c.reference": "Sahîh Muslim, 1218c",
  "src.muslim-1218c.scope": "‘Arafah and Muzdalifah as places of standing, Minâ as a place linked to the sacrifice, and elements of the Prophet’s procedure explicitly present in this variant of Jâbir’s account",
  "src.muslim-1218c.limits": "Describes the reported course of Hajj; does not on its own determine all the pillars or obligations, all the time conditions of standing at ‘Arafah, all the rules for staying at Muzdalifah or all the rules of Minâ; does not define all compensations or consequences of an omission and should not be used as a complete rule for personal cases.",
  "src.fiqh-badai-combining-travel.reference": "Bada’i as-Sana’i fi Tartib ash-Shara’i, Kitab as-Salat, conditions of the pillars of prayer",
  "src.fiqh-badai-combining-travel.scope": "Hanafi position studied: no actual combining (jam‘) of two obligatory prayers in the time of one of them for ordinary travel; textual exceptions of ‘Arafah and Muzdalifah",
  "src.fiqh-badai-combining-travel.limits": "Does not deal here with all the procedures of ‘Arafah/Muzdalifah, or every case of excuse; bringing the two prayers together at the edges of their times must be distinguished from actual jam‘.",
  "src.fiqh-dhakhira-combining-travel.reference": "Adh-Dhakhira, book of prayer, chapter on combining prayers, causes of combining",
  "src.fiqh-dhakhira-combining-travel.scope": "Maliki account studied of combining while travelling, especially while the journey continues, with internal nuances presented",
  "src.fiqh-dhakhira-combining-travel.limits": "Does not turn the reported variants into a single Maliki rule and does not cover here all the conditions of jam‘, rain, illness or other excuses.",
  "src.fiqh-majmu-combining-travel.reference": "Al-Majmu Sharh al-Muhadhdhab, book of prayer, chapter on the traveller’s prayer, combining in the time of the first or the second",
  "src.fiqh-majmu-combining-travel.scope": "Shafi‘i position studied: jam‘ possible while travelling in the time of the first or the second, with separate conditions for jam‘ taqdim and jam‘ ta’khir",
  "src.fiqh-majmu-combining-travel.limits": "Does not cover here all internal variants, all excuses other than travel or the details of personal cases.",
  "src.fiqh-mughni-combining-travel.reference": "Al-Mughni, book of prayer, chapter on the traveller’s prayer, combining two prayers while travelling",
  "src.fiqh-mughni-combining-travel.scope": "Hanbali position studied: combining while travelling permitted in the time of one of the two prayers, with specific rules on the choice of time and continuity in jam‘ taqdim",
  "src.fiqh-mughni-combining-travel.limits": "Does not cover here all the causes of combining, all the conditions of each form or all the variants attributed to Ahmad.",
  "src.fiqh-badai-latecomer.reference": "Bada’i as-Sana’i fi Tartib ash-Shara’i, Kitab as-Salat, discussion of the masbuq",
  "src.fiqh-badai-latecomer.scope": "Hanafi position studied: the latecomer follows the imam in what they join; according to Abu Hanifa and Abu Yusuf, what they join is legally the end of their prayer and what they make up is legally its beginning",
  "src.fiqh-badai-latecomer.limits": "The passage also reports internal nuances, notably a transmission from Muhammad; it should not be turned into an identical rule for all Hanafis without noting these nuances.",
  "src.fiqh-maliki-latecomer.reference": "Hashiyat as-Sawi ‘ala ash-Sharh as-Saghir, rules of the masbuq",
  "src.fiqh-maliki-latecomer.scope": "Maliki wording studied distinguishing recitation (qada) from the other actions (bina) when the latecomer completes what they missed",
  "src.fiqh-maliki-latecomer.limits": "The source is used for the distinction between words of recitation and actions; it is not here a complete inventory of every latecomer case.",
  "src.fiqh-majmu-latecomer.reference": "Al-Majmu Sharh al-Muhadhdhab, Kitab as-Salat, Bab Salat al-Jama‘a, someone who joins the last raka‘a",
  "src.fiqh-majmu-latecomer.scope": "Shafi‘i position studied: what the latecomer joins with the imam is the beginning of their own prayer and what they perform afterwards is its continuation",
  "src.fiqh-majmu-latecomer.limits": "Does not cover here every case of recitation, tashahhud, qunut or latecomers joining at other points of the raka‘a.",
  "src.fiqh-mughni-latecomer.reference": "Al-Mughni, Kitab as-Salat, Bab Sifat as-Salat, latecomer joining after the first raka‘a",
  "src.fiqh-mughni-latecomer.scope": "Hanbali account studied: in the position attributed to Ahmad in this passage, what is joined with the imam is treated as the end of the latecomer’s prayer and what they make up as its beginning",
  "src.fiqh-mughni-latecomer.limits": "The file remains limited to the passage studied and does not claim to list all of Ahmad’s transmissions or every practical case of the masbuq.",
  "src.muslim-537a.reference": "Sahîh Muslim, 537a",
  "src.muslim-537a.scope": "account of Mu‘âwiya ibn al-Hakam: people’s ordinary speech has no place in the prayer",
  "src.muslim-537a.limits": "The account teaches the rule on human speech in the prayer; the detailed consequences depending on intention, forgetfulness, ignorance and quantity are a matter of legal analysis.",
  "src.fiqh-badai-prayer-invalidators.reference": "Bada’i as-Sana’i fi Tartib ash-Shara’i, Kitab as-Salat, chapter on what invalidates the prayer",
  "src.fiqh-badai-prayer-invalidators.scope": "Hanafi passages studied on speech, deliberate hadath, eating/drinking and laughing in the prayer",
  "src.fiqh-badai-prayer-invalidators.limits": "This page does not turn the chapter’s list into a complete table of every invalidator and keeps the distinctions between deliberate acts, forgetfulness and particular cases.",
  "src.fiqh-dusuqi-prayer-invalidators.reference": "Hashiyat ad-Dusuqi ala ash-Sharh al-Kabir, chapter on what invalidates the prayer",
